<!--
  The child's position on the map.

  osmdroid's stock Marker icon is a green balloon with a pointing-hand CURSOR drawn inside it —
  on a phone that reads as a stray mouse pointer stuck to the map, and it is green next to a
  trail and an accuracy circle that are the app's violet.

  ONE path, and the hole is punched out of it with evenOdd rather than drawn over it in a second
  colour. A Drawable tint is a colour filter over the whole result, so a white centre painted on
  top would come out the same violet as the body and the pin would render as a solid blob. This
  way the single tint MapScreen applies (MapTrailHead, so the marker and the head of the trail
  are one colour) is the only colour the asset has, and the hole shows the accuracy circle
  underneath it.

  Tip at the bottom centre: the Marker is anchored ANCHOR_CENTER/ANCHOR_BOTTOM, so that point
  is the fix.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="30dp"
    android:height="40dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="32">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M12,31.5 C12,31.5 21.8,18.6 21.8,10.2 C21.8,4.8 17.4,0.5 12,0.5 C6.6,0.5 2.2,4.8 2.2,10.2 C2.2,18.6 12,31.5 12,31.5 Z M12,14.4 C9.7,14.4 7.8,12.5 7.8,10.2 C7.8,7.9 9.7,6 12,6 C14.3,6 16.2,7.9 16.2,10.2 C16.2,12.5 14.3,14.4 12,14.4 Z" />
</vector>
